## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

### 1.1 Website Name
**Cameraman Pro** (`cameraman-pro`)

### 1.2 Purpose
Cameraman Pro is a **dual-sided full-stack SaaS web application** for professional photography studios. It has two completely separate sides:

- **Public Website** — A marketing/portfolio site visible to anyone on the internet (customers, brides, families, corporate clients)
- **Studio Admin Panel** — A private, protected management dashboard visible only to the studio owner/team after logging in

Think of it like this: The public website is the **shop front**, and the admin panel is the **back office**.

### 1.3 Target Users

| User Type | Who They Are | What They Do |
|---|---|---|
| **Studio Owner** | Photographer / Business Owner | Manages all bookings, team, finance, AI tools |
| **Team Member** | Photographer, Editor, Assistant | Views assigned jobs, updates post-production |
| **Customer (Public)** | Brides, families, corporate clients | Views portfolio, books sessions, tracks order |
| **Client Portal User** | Booked customer | Logs into private portal to select photos |

### 1.4 Problem It Solves
Running a photography studio involves:
- Dozens of bookings spread across months
- Tracking who paid how much, what is pending
- Managing cameras, drones, and lenses (inventory)
- Tracking editing, album delivery, and video mixing
- Handling enquiries from potential clients
- Building a professional online presence

Most photographers use just WhatsApp + paper notebooks. **Cameraman Pro replaces all of that** with a single, smart, AI-powered platform.

### 1.5 Real-World Use Case
> Chandan Kumar Verma (Owner, Studio Cameraman Pro) receives a call from a client wanting to book a wedding shoot. Instead of writing it in a notebook, the studio manager (or BĀBU AI) creates a booking in the system — capturing client name, phone, event dates, venue, advance paid, and equipment needed. The system automatically calculates the balance due, tracks post-production editing progress, and even generates a professional PDF invoice instantly. The client can later log in via a private portal to select their favourite photos.

