## 3. FEATURES (DETAILED)

### 3.1 Core Features

#### 🗓️ Booking Management
**Why it exists:** The heartbeat of any photography business. Every client, every shoot, every rupee.

**How it works internally:**
- Admin opens `/bookings` → clicks "New Booking"
- Form captures: Client Name, Phone, Email, Address, Event Type (wedding/pre-wedding/birthday/corporate/other), Event Date(s), Venue, Equipment needed, Total package price, Advance paid
- On submit → `useBookings.addBooking()` hook fires → sanitizes all undefined values → writes to Firestore `bookings` collection
- Real-time listener (`onSnapshot`) instantly updates the bookings list without page refresh
- Booking has `status`: pending → confirmed → completed → deleted (soft delete only)
- `balanceDue = totalAmount - advancePaid` (auto-calculated)

#### 📅 Multi-Event Booking ("Sub-Events")
**Why:** Indian weddings span multiple days (Haldi, Mehendi, Baraat, Wedding, Reception).

**How:** A single booking can have a `subEvents[]` array — each with its own title, date, and time. The invoice PDF renders all sub-events as an "Event Schedule" table.

#### 💰 Financial Tracking
- `totalAmount`, `advancePaid`, `balanceDue` stored as integers in **paise** (1 INR = 100 paise) to avoid floating point bugs
- `paymentHistory[]` array logs every payment: method (cash/UPI/bank/cheque), amount, date, reference ID
- The dashboard aggregates total revenue, total collected, total pending across all bookings

#### 🎒 Inventory Management
**Why:** Cameras, drones, and lenses are expensive assets that must be tracked.

**How:**
- Each item: name, category (camera/lens/drone/lighting/tripod/accessory), status (available/booked/maintenance/damaged/deleted), serial number, purchase date, `dailyRentalRate`
- When a booking is created with equipment → that equipment's `currentBookingId` is set
- [equipmentConflict.ts](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/lib/equipmentConflict.ts) checks if a piece of gear is double-booked on the same date
- `/inventory/:id` shows full booking history and maintenance log for each item

#### 👥 Team Management
- Multi-user studio: Owner can invite team via a **6-character Studio Code** (e.g., `AB3K7Z`)
- Roles: `owner`, `admin`, `member`
- Per-booking team assignment: main photographer, drone operator, editor, assistants

#### 💸 Expense Tracking
- Log expenses: fuel, assistant payment, repair, miscellaneous
- Link an expense to a specific booking
- Analytics page shows month-over-month expense comparison

#### 🖼️ Gallery (Public Portfolio)
- Admin uploads images from `/studio-gallery`
- Images go directly to **Cloudinary** (no server needed)
- [cloudinary.ts](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/lib/cloudinary.ts) sends multipart POST to Cloudinary API with the `cameraman_gallery` upload preset
- Public `/gallery` page fetches images from Cloudinary and shows them with category filters (Wedding, Pre-Wedding, Drone, Cinematic)

#### 🤖 BĀBU AI Assistant
**The star feature.** BĀBU (Hindi word for "clerk/manager") is an LLM-powered studio intelligence assistant.

**How it works:**
- Uses **Groq API** with model `llama-3.3-70b-versatile`
- System prompt (in [groq.ts](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/lib/groq.ts)) defines BĀBU's personality: professional, bilingual (Hindi primary, English secondary), studio-aware
- Admin types a question or command in Hindi/English
- BĀBU reads live studio context (bookings, expenses, team) injected into the prompt
- BĀBU can: answer questions, extract booking details from photos/text, suggest actions, generate confirmations in Hindi

```
Example conversation:
Admin: "Kal kitne shoots hain?"
BĀBU: "कल 2 shoots हैं — Ram Sharma (Wedding, Morning Slot) और Priya Singh (Pre-Wedding, Afternoon). Total advance ₹45,000 collect हो चुका है।"
```

#### 🧠 AI Tools Suite (`/ai-tools`)
Five AI-powered tools:
1. **Quote Generator** → Input event type, duration, requirements → AI suggests package pricing
2. **Caption Generator** → Input photo description → AI writes social media captions
3. **Budget Estimator** → Input event details → AI estimates shooting budget
4. **Contract Drafter** → Input client details → AI drafts a booking contract
5. **Predictive Alerts** → [PredictiveEngine](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/lib/predictiveEngine.ts#15-268) class analyzes bookings/expenses and warns about: workload overload, equipment shortage, editor backlog, profit margin drops

#### 📄 Invoice PDF Generator
- [invoiceGenerator.ts](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/lib/invoiceGenerator.ts) uses **jsPDF** to generate professional A4 invoices client-side (no server)
- Includes: studio header, client info, event details, sub-event schedule, equipment add-ons, payment history, notes, and a branded footer
- Download instantly from the booking detail page

#### 🔗 Client Portal
- After a shoot is complete, the admin activates the client portal for a booking
- Admin sets a PIN and optionally uploads photo selection images
- Client visits `/client/login` → enters Booking ID + PIN → lands on private portal
- Client can: view their gallery link, make payment via UPI link, select favourite photos
- Portal status: `inactive` → `active` → `selections_submitted` → `album_ready`

#### 📦 Order Tracking
- Public `/track` page: customer enters their phone number or Booking ID
- System fetches booking from Firestore and shows: event date, status, post-production progress, balance due

#### 🌐 Bilingual Support (Hindi / English)
- [LanguageContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/context/LanguageContext.jsx) manages language state globally
- A language toggle button switches all UI text between English and Hindi
- Selected language stored in `localStorage` (persists across sessions)

#### 🌓 Dark / Light Mode
- `ThemeContext` in `contexts/ThemeContext.tsx` manages theme
- Toggle stored in `localStorage`

