## 8. BACKEND LOGIC

> [!NOTE]
> Cameraman Pro uses **Firebase as a serverless backend** — there is no custom Node.js/Express server. All business logic lives in the browser (custom React Hooks and lib files).

### 8.1 Routes / APIs

The app does not use traditional REST API routes. Instead:
- **Firestore** acts as the database with real-time subscriptions
- **Groq API** is called directly from the browser
- **Cloudinary** is called directly from the browser

### 8.2 Authentication System

**Step-by-step login flow:**
```
1. User visits /studio-access
2. Enters studio password (stored in .env: VITE_STUDIO_PASSWORD)
3. On success: sessionStorage.setItem("studio_access", "true")
4. StudioAccessGuard reads sessionStorage → allows access to /login
5. User clicks "Login with Google"
6. Firebase Auth: signInWithPopup(auth, new GoogleAuthProvider())
   - On Android: FirebaseAuthentication.signInWithGoogle() (native)
7. Auth state change fires: onAuthStateChanged(auth, callback)
8. AuthContext fetches user doc from Firestore users/{uid}
9. If new user:
   - generateStudioCode() → 6-char random alphanumeric (e.g. "AB3K7Z")
   - setDoc(studios/AB3K7Z, {...}) → creates studio
   - setDoc(users/{uid}, { studioId: "AB3K7Z", role: "admin" })
10. studioId stored in React context → all hooks use it for queries
```

### 8.3 Real-Time Data Flow

```typescript
// How useBookings works — the core data pattern
useEffect(() => {
  const q = query(
    collection(db, "bookings"),
    where("studioId", "==", studioId),
    orderBy("eventDate", "desc")
  );
  
  // onSnapshot = real-time listener (like WebSockets)
  const unsubscribe = onSnapshot(q, (snapshot) => {
    const bookings = snapshot.docs.map(doc => ({ id: doc.id, ...doc.data() }));
    setBookings(bookings);
  });
  
  return () => unsubscribe(); // Cleanup on unmount
}, [studioId]);
```

This means: if another team member creates a booking on their device, **all other logged-in devices update instantly** — no page refresh needed.

### 8.4 Business Logic Examples

**Soft Delete (Booking):**
```typescript
// Uses Firestore transaction to atomically:
// 1. Mark booking as "deleted"
// 2. Copy it to the "trash" collection with a 30-day expiry
const softDeleteBooking = async (booking) => {
  await runTransaction(db, async (transaction) => {
    transaction.update(bookingRef, { status: 'deleted' });
    transaction.set(trashRef, {
      ...booking,
      expiresAt: Timestamp.fromDate(new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000))
    });
  });
};
```

**Equipment Conflict Detection:**
- When booking equipment for a date, [equipmentConflict.ts](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/src/lib/equipmentConflict.ts) checks all bookings on the same date
- If a camera is already booked → show warning to admin
- This prevents scheduling the same lens for two shoots on the same day

**Predictive Engine:**
```typescript
// PredictiveEngine class in predictiveEngine.ts
const engine = new PredictiveEngine(bookings, expenses, inventory);
const alerts = engine.analyze();
// Returns alerts like:
// { type: 'workload', title: '⚠️ अगले 7 दिनों में 5 shoots!', severity: 'warning' }
// { type: 'equipment_shortage', title: '🚨 Camera shortage on 2026-06-15!' }
// { type: 'profit_drop', title: '📉 Profit margin सिर्फ 18% है!' }
```

