## 10. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION

### 10.1 Speed Improvements

| Technique | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Vite bundler** | Extremely fast dev server (HMR in <100ms), optimized production builds |
| **Code splitting** | React Router v6 supports lazy loading per route |
| **Tree shaking** | Vite eliminates unused code from bundles |
| **Amounts in paise** | Integer math is faster and avoids float precision issues |

### 10.2 Data / Caching

| Technique | How |
|---|---|
| **Real-time listeners** | Firestore `onSnapshot` caches data client-side. Subsequent reads are instant from local cache |
| **Firestore offline support** | Firestore SDK has built-in offline persistence — data available offline |
| **Language preference** | `localStorage` saves language/theme — no refetch needed |
| **Client-side filtering** | After initial data load, filtering/sorting happens in React state (no new DB query) |

### 10.3 Image Optimization

- All images served via **Cloudinary CDN** — auto-format (WebP when supported), auto-quality, responsive sizing via Cloudinary transformations
- Cloudinary uses global edge servers — images load fast worldwide

### 10.4 PDF Generation

- Invoice PDF is generated **client-side** using jsPDF — zero server load, instant download

---

## 11. SCALABILITY

### 11.1 How It Handles More Users

| Component | Scalability |
|---|---|
| **Firestore** | Google-managed, horizontally scales automatically to millions of documents |
| **Firebase Auth** | Google-managed authentication, scales to millions of users |
| **Cloudinary** | CDN with global edge nodes — handles millions of image requests |
| **Groq API** | Managed AI inference — scales via Groq's infrastructure |
| **Netlify** | CDN-based hosting — React SPA served from edge, no server to scale |
| **Capacitor (Android)** | App runs on device — no additional server load |

### 11.2 Multi-Studio SaaS Architecture

The database is **already designed for SaaS**:
- Every document has a `studioId`
- Security rules enforce isolation
- To onboard a new studio: just one `setDoc(studios/newCode, ...)` call

This means 100 studios or 10,000 studios can use the same system without any architectural changes.

### 11.3 Firestore Scaling Considerations

- Complex queries use **Firestore Composite Indexes** ([firestore.indexes.json](file:///c:/Users/Play%20Edit%20Solution/Desktop/Cameraman%20Pro/firestore.indexes.json))
- Currently: bookings ordered by `eventDate desc` filtered by `studioId` — needs an index
- For large studios (10,000+ bookings): consider pagination using Firestore `startAfter()`

### 11.4 Future Scaling

- Add **Firebase Cloud Functions** for server-side operations (webhooks, automated WhatsApp messages, scheduled reports)
- Add **Razorpay/PhonePe** payment gateway for online payments
- Add **Redis caching** layer via Cloud Functions for heavy analytics queries

