## 13. DEPLOYMENT

### 13.1 Development Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd cameraman-pro

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Create .env file in root
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
VITE_CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_cloudinary_key
VITE_CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_secret
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=cameraman_gallery
VITE_STUDIO_PASSWORD=your_studio_password

# 4. Start development server
npm run dev
# Opens at http://localhost:5173

# 5. Build for production
npm run build
# Output in /dist folder
```

### 13.2 Firebase Setup

```bash
# Install Firebase CLI
npm install -g firebase-tools

# Login
firebase login

# Initialize project
firebase init

# Deploy Firestore rules & indexes
firebase deploy --only firestore

# Deploy to Firebase Hosting (optional alternative to Netlify)
firebase deploy --only hosting
```

### 13.3 Netlify Deployment

```
1. Push code to GitHub
2. Connect GitHub repo to Netlify
3. Build settings:
   - Build command: npm run build
   - Publish directory: dist
4. Add all VITE_ environment variables in Netlify dashboard
5. Deploy! Netlify auto-deploys on every `git push`
```

### 13.4 Android Build (Capacitor)

```bash
# Add Android platform
npx cap add android

# Build web app
npm run build

# Sync web code to Android
npx cap sync android

# Open in Android Studio
npx cap open android

# Build APK from Android Studio → Build → Build APK
```

